From 2c7efe226a94c683b0e7d34106dc69c68a2d2e5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 19:41:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] experiments/libhegel-vs-hegel-c: the graph pair under nofork
 + HEGEL_ISOLATED

The comparison measures nofork + HEGEL_ISOLATED on the crash pair only,
one draw per case (19 ms against fork mode's 31).  The graph pair, where
fork mode pays a pipe round trip for each of many draws per case (1850 ms
against nofork's 76), has no isolated row, so what crash isolation costs
for a draw-heavy generator is not in the table.

hc_graph_iso.c is hc_graph.c with the nofork runner and adj_build + its
assert inside a HEGEL_ISOLATED block; run.sh prints it as
"3 graph / hegel-c nofork+ISOLATED" and counts its lines.

The row is not measured yet: the Results block in README.md and the
figures in docs/libhegel-vs-hegel-c.md are as they were.  After
make -C experiments/libhegel-vs-hegel-c run, paste the new output and say
in the "Fork mode time" paragraph what the row shows (expected from the
crash pair's ~0.25 ms per fork: a few hundred ms).

Not built or run: written in a sandbox that could not build the
repository (gcc -fsyntax-only -Wall -Wextra is clean).

